# Dingle's countdown (context/community_circuits/Fixed_Textscrn_countdown.txt) with zero-padded minutes and seconds:
# it used to show 1:9 for 69 s, now 01:09. Five parts added at the end; everything else is Dingle's, credit note kept.
# Tested in sandbox/dingle_countdown.sbx.
name dingle_countdown_padded
box countdown
label in0 Terminal
label in2 Auto restart
label in1 Reset button
label out1 sprinkler
label out0 textscrn
c mod0 mod Modulus=60
c osc1 osc
c mem2 mem Value=0
c sub3 sub
c div4 div
c mem5 mem Value=60
c floor6 floor
c mul7 mul
c relay8 relay IsOn=false
c check9 check Output=120 FalseOutput="" TargetSignal=1
c concat10 concat Separator=:
c delay11 delay Delay=0.009999999776482582
w mem5.out div4.2 mul7.2
w div4.out floor6.in
w mul7.out check9.set_output
w in0 mul7.1
w concat10.out out0
w in1 check9.in
w check9.out mem2.in
w delay11.out mod0.in div4.1 mem2.in
w sub3.out delay11.in
w osc1.out relay8.1
w relay8.signal_out1 sub3.2
w mem2.out relay8.2 relay8.set_state
w relay8.signal_out2 sub3.1
note "Made by dingle" "Please don't delete this, I would like to be credited for my time. I encorage downloading blueprint mod to save this and use on other servers! I have cheaper versions and vanilla versions. Msg me on discord @sirdinglebear"
note Blueprints "Circuit made with Blueprints. \n \n Get it now on the steam workshop!"
note "PADDING (added)" "concat(0, n), then the regex (.{2})$ keeps the last two characters: 9 -> 09, 12 -> 12."
c z mem Value=0
c pm concat
c ps concat
c rm regex Expression="(.{2})$" UseCaptureGroup=true Output=1 FalseOutput=""
c rs regex Expression="(.{2})$" UseCaptureGroup=true Output=1 FalseOutput=""
w z.out pm.1 ps.1
w floor6.out pm.2
w mod0.out ps.2
w pm.out rm.in
w ps.out rs.in
w rm.out concat10.1
w rs.out concat10.2
